Subject: Protect words near digits in LLMLingua-2 _main_compressor

When force_reserve_digit=True and the PromptCompressor instance has a
non-zero `_digit_neighbor_radius` attribute, also force-keep the N words
to the left and right of every digit-containing word. Mirrors the legacy
patch from cuddly-prism plan §"LLMLingua-2 源码修改".

Apply with:
    cd $(python -c "import llmlingua, os; print(os.path.dirname(llmlingua.__file__))")
    patch -p1 < /path/to/0001-digit-neighbor-radius.patch

Idempotent guard: re-applying is detected by apply_patch.py via marker
"_digit_neighbor_radius" in prompt_compressor.py.
---
--- a/prompt_compressor.py
+++ b/prompt_compressor.py
@@ -2404,13 +2404,27 @@
                         new_token_probs, int(100 * reduce_rate + 1)
                     )

+                    if force_reserve_digit:
+                        digit_neighbor_radius = getattr(self, '_digit_neighbor_radius', 0)
+                        if digit_neighbor_radius > 0:
+                            _protected = set()
+                            for _i, _w in enumerate(words):
+                                if bool(re.search(r'\d', _w)):
+                                    for _off in range(-digit_neighbor_radius, digit_neighbor_radius + 1):
+                                        if 0 <= _i + _off < len(words):
+                                            _protected.add(_i + _off)
+                        else:
+                            _protected = set()
+                    else:
+                        _protected = set()
+
